 at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/7e4d38e401c4ce01330d6082dadd43e50974a55b666023d8b8d51bbcbc7f7258.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250753 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4b5807f-a10a-518a-84fa-907bf699884c" :knowledge-point/title "Exponential Functions With Vertical Reflections and Horizontal Shifts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8388a33b-22d2-5fb1-86f9-a8c8acd14617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/d968dcdb24e3e5538ccbe51ec4c2a94b8f8e4b23b585810a3d24fcbf255e15ed.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250755} {:answer/id #uuid "454f4243-d973-5d75-bce9-5b9645ae749d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/f5643bb8e251468bea69940e4c0335739096d371e36ab569d898b8675da5f3a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250756} {:answer/id #uuid "676ebe2c-eea9-52a7-90e7-255ba85486f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/51b6901035dee1fe0ba56eb7b06b1ca0d43a1edf612cfff23ea44383b8bdd312.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250757} {:answer/id #uuid "dc628fdc-80fb-5ca9-ac4f-a512cbc295e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/2fddab60da44e86e5c99f9f2933145602a1aa8660140488a9ce2da42aab5900a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250758} {:answer/id #uuid "6a79fd21-b63e-5b01-b69a-03001ca14ce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/1ab4f9a548004379156deb2f1e152a16b88b585ee7d576674d394cf96c5bca20.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "676ebe2c-eea9-52a7-90e7-255ba85486f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/51b6901035dee1fe0ba56eb7b06b1ca0d43a1edf612cfff23ea44383b8bdd312.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250757} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc4a7917-bfac-5f07-a862-179264752e4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250754}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a41594a-f79c-59b8-b328-4364bfa01e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-317898" :question/problem "Which of the following is the graph of  $y=-{(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x+1}?$" :question/worked-solution "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/a9b6c2b12c1bc4bc7794dd5d409a99c61bf256ea58f9a016657cbbea5ef6b1e4.png)\n\n \n\n- Horizontally shift it by $1$ units to the left to give $y={(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x+1}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(-1,1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/5f4c0e3c4573f6e3167390d54ee21bbb8bf6e3879fcc06e7adf9d311e80ccb62.png)\n\n- Then, reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{(\\frac{3}{10})}^{x+1}.$ The point $(-1,1)$ moves to $(-1,-1)$ and the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/b541282b8661f2fb28d0ce1f10c22a9a8cc7b083460c05093a89722bc084d7b9.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186217735 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fa86dd3-3bb3-54d5-8940-5dc07ae4c99f" :knowledge-point/title "Exponential Growth Functions With Horizontal and Vertical Shifts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-fi