6493839db2b86dac7b73d64f058c9c185c6ef6717b9937a286dd96b46b3d14.png)\n\n- To plot $y={3}^{x-3},$ we shift the graph of $y={3}^{x}$ horizontally by $3$ units to the right. The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(3,1),$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/1a8c220f94fdea96374a3a336d6262c4a272f4b630749dbf51c33bccf42ef46c.png)\n\n- To plot $y={3}^{x-3}-2,$ we shift the graph of $y={3}^{x-3}$ vertically by $2$ units down. The point $(3,1)$ moves to $(3,-1)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/65a4e59ccc4bae7f2de681ce4820020a180d087c5257b6b41dd8830bee587230.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250760 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5fa86dd3-3bb3-54d5-8940-5dc07ae4c99f" :knowledge-point/title "Exponential Growth Functions With Horizontal and Vertical Shifts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3caae5a5-bb1d-5e81-9833-73c8590dfb7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/b42fceffe3323cd1eaae2a76d0e108b66ddcdb9f9ce541dd668cde74d321ab07.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250762} {:answer/id #uuid "e8e4a1bb-5a6b-5f1c-b528-bbc57e56d87e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/de4e40f6b409bc88c3336e243e68ea7192f9cde4fe6021940f9767b856179296.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250763} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f3310c-421c-5482-9023-9f56fa999613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943741/assets/5eb8b9ec060564ea5e59191be7a6f9e9932634d8ca26a95e35e7db1d1f27c004.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250764} {:answer/id 